+# Editorial notebook direction — 2 October 2026
+
+This replaces the rejected dark control-stack design. The actual before capture is ../evidence-redesign/before.png on emulator-5564; it is historical baseline evidence, not acceptance. The optional new-ui-direction skill is absent.
+
+Research opens with a compact PocketLore masthead and offline indicator, an editorial title, a prominent inset question composer and one forest-green action. Real installed collections and recent persisted research occupy separate sections below it. No synthetic topics, histories, counts or maps are permitted. Completed answers replace the empty introduction, retaining visible outcome uncertainty and individually inspectable source quotations. Technical model/import/storage controls remain in Settings.
+
+The four destinations are Research, Library, Explore and Saved. Original line icons supplement readable labels; selection has shape and text state. Library is a searchable source index; Explore searches actual installed place records and clearly states unavailable routing/current hours. Saved uses title-first notebook rows with metadata and disclosed record actions rather than stacks of equally prominent buttons. Source reading preserves bookmarks, notes, comparison, text size, theme and portable export. Back returns to the initiating work.
+
+Warm paper #F7F4EC, ink #202621, secondary #59635B, forest #245B43 and pale surface #EEEEE5 define the light default. Titles use Android serif, body/control text Android sans. Body >=16sp, source 18sp by default, headings 28–34sp, 24dp outer gutters, 8/12/16/24/32dp rhythm. All hit regions >=48dp, wrap long titles, visible focus border, no fixed body heights. Navigation reflows at large font sizes and hides with the keyboard. Insets protect system bars/IME. Contrast is calculated from actual tokens before delivery; runtime geometry is measured, not inferred from declarations.
+
+Empty states offer a real next action; loading uses actual operation state without percentages; errors preserve questions/data; cancelled results remain labelled; restored snapshots retain identity and source access. Source dates and rights live in source details, while result uncertainty stays beside the result. No answer/evidence policy, rights, pack format or inference changes are in scope.
+
+Primary research: Android core quality https://developer.android.com/docs/quality-guidelines/core-app-quality ; Views accessibility https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/accessibility/views/apps-views ; Material canonical layouts https://m3.material.io/foundations/layout/canonical-examples/overview ; Apple typography https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/typography . The inspected competitor MOBILE-DESIGN-RESEARCH.md derives task-first navigation, 48dp targets, 4.5:1 body contrast, scaling and state retention from these sources. Android measurements govern this implementation; no rival code or visual assets are copied.
+
+Native integration is limited to the exact two CMake linker changes accepted in canonical task305 at b1c20ced202c7b3ae957b2ee0c32e3f999f91750. Packaged ELF LOAD/RELRO and ZIP alignment plus API37 loader state must be evidenced. No compatibility-mode override, generation, corpus download, canonical mutation or use of 5560/5562.
+
+Verification: matching viewport before/after on existing 5564, source and persisted Saved roundtrip, keyboard/Back, enlarged type, cancelled/error/empty states, APK/native hashes and bounded build logs. Development tests and screenshots do not establish physical/human acceptance or competitor superiority. Remaining competitor capabilities stay explicitly pending in UI-CAPABILITY-GAPS.md.
+
+## Measured implementation rules
+
+The actual token pairs measured by tools/evaluation/check_ui_scope.py are ink/paper 14.04:1, ink/surface 13.23:1, forest/paper 7.20:1, forest/surface 6.78:1, secondary/paper 5.69:1 and secondary/surface 5.36:1. These are token contrast measurements, not a complete assistive-technology audit. Native button elevation is removed; keyboard focus receives a 3dp forest outline. Body text remains >=16sp. Runtime reports measure clickable targets, including the settings icon; screenshots use the device's unchanged 1280×2856 viewport.
+
+Collection cards use actual active PackLibrary identities and open edition details; the bundled Water science card leads to Library's actual TSV source passages. Imported bulk source searches retain their existing APIs and generation restrictions. No source card silently scopes the research engine. Recent cards select only persisted research records. Saved search updates actual SQLite results, record actions are disclosed, and reader scroll position persists by record/comparison identity.
