+# Native UI refinement: capability boundary
+
+The competitor-feature audit completed at 2026-10-01T21:41:40Z. Its actual `repo/output/HANDOFF.json`, 63-entry features.json, matrix and design/extras documents were read. This lane verified their declared artifact hashes and all 78 unique cited primary-source file hashes, and inspected relevant persistence, reader and export source excerpts. Receipts are in lane evidence-refined/competitor-audit-receipt.json and competitor-source-check.json. The audit is static source/documentation research: no rival APK behavior or performance was reproduced. It reports an initial accidental tracked-asset download and subsequent source-only cleanup; this UI lane did not repeat that acquisition. Bounty data returned 403, so exhaustive current submissions are not established.
+
+Pinned revisions: AndroidLM `5abca020a65dea01a04d52131943e440a5e6f5cf`; BOAR `0cfd4a77badd01297af8dc9a3a10924f8a895105`; upstream Field Atlas `fc6092530f647fd34a665b4924a4a91341eccf66`; Field Atlas vector-search fork `769e85d162f266d9abf831134b4e149175d4dcfe`. The audit examined an older PocketLore baseline; the mapping below updates only this refinement's concrete scope and does not claim the whole union is implemented.
+
+Primary references checked on 2026-10-01:
+
+- [Field Atlas fork](https://github.com/vbuterin/fieldatlas), with upstream [Field Atlas](https://github.com/0x94t3z/fieldatlas): locally verified packs, citation inspection, privacy/diagnostics, model unloading, optional semantic/vector retrieval and audio tooling are described. This UI lane adds notebook workflows; it does not reproduce those retrieval or audio capabilities or validate the reported physical-device claims.
+- [AndroidLM](https://github.com/Phineas1500/AndroidLM): documented broad offline reference/travel sources, location-aware place recommendations, domain reference material and streamed expert-model execution. PocketLore's city/category search remains source-record browsing, without routing, verified current hours, diet suitability, GPS, or a comparable qualified model. No phone speed or answer-quality comparison was run.
+- [BOAR](https://github.com/rferrari/boar-app): documented personal document ingestion, collection export, model selection and multilingual UI. PocketLore exports saved notebook snapshots, not a new ingestible knowledge-pack format; arbitrary PDF/document ingestion and localization are still missing. BOAR's first-run networking design is not adopted.
+
+## Implemented in this lane
+
+- Native Research, Library, Places and Saved destinations, with model/import/storage controls in secondary Settings or disclosure.
+- Private SQLite history of completed research and opened sources, persistent bookmarks and notes, searchable titles/questions/notes, deletion confirmation and explicit storage bounds.
+- Full-screen saved source/result reading, persisted 18/22/26sp sizing, navy and cream reader themes, dates and original provenance, with no inference or rights promotion.
+- Comparison of two actual saved records or two actual retrieved source passages; this presents evidence without generating a comparative answer.
+- Portable UTF-8 Markdown snapshot/notebook export through the Android document picker, and read-granted content-URI sharing through the system chooser.
+
+These statements describe implemented code. Runtime evidence and exact candidate identities are recorded separately; documentation itself is not execution proof.
+
+## Remaining product and acceptance gaps
+
+| Capability | Remaining boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| Research usefulness | Canonical answer repair is outside this lane; saved weak/abstained results retain their labels. |
+| Follow-up dialogue and projects | No conversational reasoning state, notebook folders, tags, or cross-record synthesis. |
+| Source search | Existing title/FTS readers retained; no new semantic search, article-specific find, OCR, PDF ingestion or document conversion. |
+| Places | No map renderer, routing, GPS, live opening hours, verified diet/accessibility or deduplicated venue guarantee. |
+| Coverage | Only installed editions are searched; staged host assets and database counts are not content completeness or rights clearance. |
+| Reading | Native single-column reading; no rich equation renderer or fully adaptive tablet split-pane workspace. |
+| Portability | Markdown export is not pack import, notebook re-import, sync, encrypted backup or interoperability certification. |
+| Sharing | No compatible receiver on this AOSP emulator; chooser/provider checks cannot prove recipient delivery. |
+| Accessibility | Runtime text scaling and node bounds are bounded checks; TalkBack listening, switch access and human accessibility acceptance remain open. |
+| Hardware | Emulator results do not establish physical Android/GrapheneOS, thermals, memory safety, battery or 12GB-phone acceptance. |
+| Competition | No matched device/corpus/question comparison and no superiority claim. |
+
+
