@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Editorial notebook verification
+
+This candidate replaces the rejected refined dark UI. DIRECTION-2.md was written before implementation. The baseline image and stage1 after image are actual emulator-5564 captures at the same viewport; final runtime captures supersede stage1. Prior refined handoffs and their criticisms remain historical. No screenshot alone establishes completion.
+
+The private source base remains 15c48b43999cb57599c58477668fc73a03748276 on codex/pocketlore-ui, actual Git directory ../checkpoint.git, with read-only metadata. Stage1, stage2 and stage3 nonempty patches and file hashes are retained under ../evidence-redesign. Coordinator sealing is required; no invented commit or empty checkpoint is reported.
+
+The design uses original native Views and line icons, no rival code or assets. Research has a single composer, edition-aware bookshelf and real recent research; Library now reads the bundled USGS source passages as well as existing bulk searches; Explore retains actual place search and truthful unavailable routing/hours; Saved retains local records, bookmarks, notes, comparison and export. Source reading supports text sizing, light/dark preference and persistent position. Technical model/import/storage controls remain in Settings. Result text and uncertainty still come from the unchanged answer engine.
+
+Build uses the rig JDK/SDK and cached Gradle, offline, 2 workers, 2 GiB Gradle heap. Native inputs are the four exact binaries extracted from accepted305 APK 9ce430ec0dcf9c4cb5fa537d9b3bcc2cdf197fe59b4121aee54fefa0a7079e92; the accepted two CMake target changes are included verbatim. This is verified binary reuse, not a claimed clean native recompilation. Native-source/build input identities, accepted commit and binary hashes are in native-inputs.json. No old unaligned binary is intentionally shipped. The actual APK is inspected for ELF LOAD/RELRO and ZIP alignment. API37 runtime verifies native session creation/cancellation/close and SQLite query, without generation.
+
+Runtime instrumentation uses only existing emulator-5564 after boot and active-instrumentation checks. The coordinator's sprint receipt reports the GPU renderer; this lane did not restart/wipe/create any emulator or touch 5560/5562. Tests use real bundled groundwater source data, real SQLite notebook records, actual Android SAF and content provider, source rights/date retention, restored question/result, Settings/Back, keyboard, 100%/200% font scale and absent Places coverage. Test-created notes explicitly identify UI verification. Research runs with no loaded model and verifies invokedModel=false; no inference or download is performed. Global font scale is restored afterward.
+
+Limits: these are emulator development checks, not physical Android/GrapheneOS, TalkBack traversal, human usability, rival parity or research-quality acceptance. Active-generation cancellation is not newly exercised because this UI sprint prohibits inference; existing engine cancellation code is unchanged. SAF cancellation is exercised. Full-data303 evidence belongs to API35 emulator-5562: 41,628,602,368 final data/code bytes, 43,145,453,568 measured replacement bytes and 44,796,211,667 calculated provider/reserve bound. None is a 5564 capacity receipt. Bulk source reading remains inherited code and must be integrated against real installed bulk assets separately. No canonical330 personal-document feature is included or claimed.
+
+Remaining capabilities are reconciled in UI-CAPABILITY-GAPS.md. Markdown export is portable text, not a verified notebook reimport format. Comparison presents two actual saved snapshots and does not generate a new synthesis. Source snapshots preserve rights labels but grant no new rights. Notebook limits remain 200 records, 2 MiB per record, 16 MiB body/provenance; notes and metadata add overhead. Physical resource budget and independent final integration remain open.
+
+The cold-restart driver initially failed because Android correctly refused shell access to a non-exported Saved Activity, then because an external Main launch retained the existing task's top screen. Both failures are preserved. The repaired driver uses visible Research/Saved navigation and actual touch coordinates from the current hierarchy; it verifies notebook rows after process restart, reopens the source, dismisses the keyboard with Back, and compares the installed APK bytes with the built APK. No Activity was made exported to accommodate testing.
+
+The populated Research state collapses the introductory composer into a question heading and Edit question action; the original engine output and uncertainty stay visible, with source excerpts in separate cards. The source-unavailable screen has a visible Close reader action before asynchronous loading completes. Loading labels follow real operations; no artificial waiting or fake percentage is used to make a loading screenshot.
+
+The delivery-state test found a real second-recreation failure: changing from a restored result to editing stopped the snapshot from being saved. Both failed 100%/200% reports and their exact APK are retained. Explicit snapshot tracking now preserves the editing state and clears the old snapshot when new research begins. The regression checks compact result → Edit question → changed draft → Activity recreation, ensuring the prior answer is not relabeled or displayed as an answer to that draft. Final receipts must come from the repaired runs, not the failed delivery runs.
